Two things the table view withholds that `board` shows:

1. `karr board` writes `@bob` behind a held card; `karr list` prints `#1 in-progress First task [high, blocked]` and nothing about who holds it. kanban-md's table has ID, STATUS, PRIORITY, TITLE, CLAIMED, TAGS, DUE. An agent choosing what to touch has to go through `--json` to learn that a card is taken.

2. On this board today `karr list` prints only `0 task(s)`; `karr board` says `263 tasks (263 done hidden)`. The list line reads as an empty board.

## What to build

- Table: show the claim (`@bob` in the meta bracket, or a CLAIMED column; pick what keeps rows under 80 columns; tags are opt-in via `board --tags`, follow that precedent if a column is too wide). Whether `--compact` grows `@bob` is the decision `board --compact` already made; check it and stay consistent.
- Footer: when the default filter hid finished cards, say so: `0 task(s) (263 done hidden; --status done to include)`. Only when something was hidden; `--json` untouched.

Changes entry, tests against the fixtures list already has.

